","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-02T10:34:59Z"},{"id":3738612601,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7e1rN5","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/96648715?u=af70f5d107e9c1447f296643d5a566dab53d25e8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AThousandShips","id":96648715,"node_id":"U_kgDOBcK-Cw","login":"AThousandShips","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AThousandShips"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-3738612601","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-02-02T10:37:44Z"},{"id":3747197896,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7fWbPI","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/3255568?u=4730e9a35d4b60504321a720796615a705462cef&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Naros","id":3255568,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjMyNTU1Njg=","login":"Naros","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Naros"},"body":"I'll defer to AThousandShips on the language, but LGTM.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-3747197896","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-03T19:36:50Z"},{"id":3866166510,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7mcQTu","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","login":"AdriaandeJongh","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh"},"body":"Played around with this and think this is a great feature in general. A few notes:\r\n\r\n- I was unable to raise the sticky count above 6. Why not? IMO it should be able to go to a large number just because it will enable this UX improvement on various specific workflows. Even in Rift Riff's settings screen I easily hit 6 layers of organization deep and it wasn't enough. I suggest having a maximum of 16.\r\n\r\n- Looking at the trees in my commercial-game-grade projects, I think the default maximum sticky items of 3 is too low making the sticky headers less useful than they can be. The point of that number is to avoid infinite sticky items and filling the entire panel with stickies making the panel unusable.\r\n-- It's not trivial to land on a better number without making assumptions about some sort of median height of Godot user's scene panel.\r\n-- ... but making assumptions based on my experience with the editor, `5` would be a better default.\r\n\r\n- I'm not sure yet whether this should be improved and how it even could be improved, but at the core of the sticky header is that it 'hides' all the in-between nodes that are not the shortest path to root. However, there is currently no visual indication of _when there are_ nodes in between the sticky ones or not. For example, in the video below, there is no visual indication that Control1 exists when Control2 sticks to the top:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/5d185d58-7d1b-4acb-8131-6a51574bc39f\r\n\r\nBut like I said, I'm not sure we can and should address this. My first thought would be to add a tiny indicator like this one <img width=\"21\" height=\"26\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/33c42bdb-a05e-43d6-ae8a-ad2b6674d81b\" /> and stick it in between all the edges that hide nodes... but it'll very soon can crammed with all those icons, so I don't even like that solution much.\r\n\r\n- And finally, here's a few screenshots of a bunch of trees in Rift Riff showing how much more readable the tree becomes after this change – as well as notice that a few more stickied items above 6 would have been convenient for us:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"308\" height=\"212\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d05174d6-ddbe-4054-a886-b5745e0261f6\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"316\" height=\"246\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/eb7d63cc-0395-4c6d-95ab-02fa94f5b474\" />\r\n\r\n<img width=\"314\" height=\"271\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/c1adf10f-e8e3-4c42-9316-29781d107e1f\" />","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-3866166510","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-27T10:26:48Z"},{"id":3866181638,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7mcUAG","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","login":"AdriaandeJongh","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-3866181638","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-27T10:30:08Z"},{"id":3866191004,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7mcWSc","state":"COMMENTED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","login":"AdriaandeJongh","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh"},"body":"","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-3866191004","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-27T10:32:56Z"},{"id":3870371695,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7msS9v","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5611323?v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/AdriaandeJongh","id":5611323,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MTEzMjM=","login":"AdriaandeJongh","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/AdriaandeJongh"},"body":"Regardless of my comment above, which may or may not improve the usability of this feature only ever so slightly, I think this is a great usability feature. Tested it and works fantastic IMO – this is the kind of feature you didn't know you missed until you try it. Some people might hate it, but they can easily turn it off.\n\nI didn't look at the code; someone else will have to chime in there.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-3870371695","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-02-28T10:57:45Z"},{"id":3882924207,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7ncLiv","state":"APPROVED","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/60579014?u=ec87bf81cd2f5f0947670400f48cf0845c25d719&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/passivestar","id":60579014,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYwNTc5MDE0","login":"passivestar","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/passivestar"},"body":"Tested, works as expected. Been thinking for a while that this would be nice to have.","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-3882924207","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","submitted_at":"2026-03-03T14:29:06Z"},{"id":4077344695,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc7zB1e3","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"56a02831e75e4eb170093db8c208f42515b42eae","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/180032?u=68d23e7ee9cdf810da125e8510b72f845b9dccc8&v=4","created_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","followers":0,"following":0,"html_url":"https://github.com/Calinou","id":180032,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE4MDAzMg==","login":"Calinou","type":"User","owned_private_repos":0,"public_gists":0,"public_repos":0,"total_private_repos":0,"url":"https://api.github.com/users/Calinou"},"body":"Tested locally, it works as expected.\r\n\r\nNote that the rebase is non-trivial, as the the Tree drop indicator PR was recently merged.\r\n\r\nSome feedback:\r\n\r\n- Right-clicking a sticky item should probably *not* scroll to it, so that you can open the context menu related to the item without scrolling up. Only left-clicking a sticky item should scroll to it.\r\n\r\n- Selecting items with the arrow keys can leave the selected item invisible:\r\n\r\nhttps://github.com/user-attachments/assets/0add3ec7-7c87-43c7-ab28-ced0fe60ca6d\r\n\r\n- I'm concerned about the usable height of the Tree potentially decreasing a lot in certain scenes. This is particularly a problem on displays where vertical screen real estate is at a premium, such as 16:9 laptops, Macs with the Dock always visible (the default), and so on.\r\n\r\n  - A breadcrumbs solution similar to what VS Code features at the top of the file view might be preferable for this. It lets you show multiple node names on the same line, provided the inspector is width enough. If there isn't enough space, then we can compact the display by showing only the first letters of each node name, or possibly just show the node icon.\r\n\r\nRough mockup of what it'd look like:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"276\" height=\"240\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/4159a649-a8d1-4f81-b7ca-1fe47710313b\" />\r\n\r\n  - Perhaps we should show just *one* sticky item, which would be the direct parent of the currently selected node. This would be helpful in long lists of sibling nodes, but wouldn't trade up too much vertical space. VS Code also does this with the function signature as seen in this screenshot:\r\n\r\n<img width=\"327\" height=\"94\" alt=\"Image\" src=\"https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/d80c00fa-a2de-4776-b65d-760fbff10c42\" />","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/115697#pullrequestreview-4077344695","pull_request_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/115697","author_association":"MEMBER","submitted_at":"2026-04-08T18:28:58Z"},{"id":4135196431,"node_id":"PRR_kwDOAO6SJc72ehcP","state":"COMMENTED","commit_id":"ef7260eaaabf317c3d29c8fd79c822c1489ffcae","user":{"site_admin":false,"suspended":false,"updated_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2223172?u=fc85633b469acb6e7baef4dba5171f19